      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-38324",
      ":question/problem": "The size of a bush growing in a schoolyard is being monitored. The area $A\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}$ of the bush at any given moment grows at a rate that's directly proportional to the area at that moment. Additionally, $2\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}$ of the bush is cut away every month.\nWhat is the differential equation that describes the rate of change in the area of the schoolyard bush at time $t,$ where $t$ is the time in months since it started growing?"
