      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-38325",
      ":question/problem": "A scientist is monitoring bacteria in a flask. The number of bacteria $B(t)$ in the flask grows at a rate that's proportional to the square of the time $t$, in seconds. Additionally, $550$ bacteria are added into the flask each second.\nWhat is the differential equation that describes the rate of change in the population of bacteria at time $t$, where $t$ is the time (in seconds) since bacteria was first added to the flask?"
