      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-51252",
      ":question/problem": "A tank is being filled with water. The rate of change of the volume of water in the tank $V,$ in milliliters, due to inflow is directly proportional to the time $t,$ measured in hours, with positive constant of proportionality $k$. Additionally, the tank is also leaking $200\\,\\text{ml}$ of water every hour. What is the differential equation that describes the rate of change of the volume of water in the tank, at time $t,$ where $t$ is the time (in hours) since the tank started filling?"
